text:
Tsar Dušan,

I ask for mercy

for the stoned women,

for their accomplice dark nights,

for the scent of clover and branches

where they fell intoxicated

like quails or koalas,

for their despised lives,

for the compassion that their pains

of love did not receive.

I ask for mercy

for the moonlight and rubies

of their skin,

for their twilights,

for the rains of loosened hair,

for the silver branches of their arms,

for their stripped

and accursed loves:

for the Mary Magdalenes.
